{
  "case_id": "2002-01-729",
  "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2002-01-729",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Alaska's Megan's Law makes available to members of the public who seek it certain truthful information about convicted sex offenders. The State makes this information available to help protect against the risk that the convicted sex offender will offend again."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2002-01-729",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One -- one line that I -- I think there is respondents seek to establish in this case is that this information has to be generated by acts that occur after the conviction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2002-01-729",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They do not. It clearly --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2002-01-729",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Roberts, the only challenge in this case is to the retroactivity. Is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2002-01-729",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is our test for whether it rises to the level of punishment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2002-01-729",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress and the legislatures of 50 States have agreed that citizens should have access to truthful information concerning the identity and location of convicted sex offenders."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2002-01-729",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We believe that the Alaska Sex Offender Registration Act imposes punishment because it possesses three features which are classically considered to be punishment, and not like any other civil or regulatory measure this Court has seen before."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2002-01-729",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First of all, the sanction attaches automatically and inescapably solely on a basis of a prior conviction, without any determination of present dangerousness at all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-01-729",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They do, and -- and they're required to -- on their quarterly report to report any changes in their physical characteristics, they gain weight, they grow gray hair, they get lasik surgery, don't have glasses, grow a beard, get fat."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-729",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But we're here today on an ex post facto question before the Court, and the question is, is it punishment, or is it not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-01-729",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0001-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "conviction and tacking on certain responsibilities to the prior conviction as opposed to really trying to fit the goal here of protecting the public from dangerous people."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Thompson",
      "case_id": "2002-01-729",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And that's why I keep going back to the concept of probation and parole because historically there's no dispute that probation is a depravation of liberty. Not -- it's not like going to jail, but it's a depravation of liberty. And -- and it's been considered as punishment, and that's what this thing does to people."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2002-01-729",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question, Justice Kennedy, is not whether it's burdensome to require someone to fill out a form and verify it. The question is, is that so punitive that you"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Roberts",
      "case_id": "2002-01-729",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think it is very important to place the various points that have been touched on this morning in the proper legal framework."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2002-01-729",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1a9c7ac55a566d481cea94350eaef6b4e96b518768b1d3633069c877da2e5e2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1a9c7ac55a5-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: Thank you, Mr. Roberts.\nThe case is submitted.\n(Whereupon, at 11:03 a.m., the case in the\nabove-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
